ENGLISH TERMS - AUTHORITATIVE VERSION

This license sets out separate terms for original Motive project code,
texture assets, and model assets. Third-party materials remain subject to
their respective licenses. This license does not alter their ownership or
licensing terms.

1. Project Code

Permission is granted to use, copy, modify, and distribute the project code
without requesting separate permission, subject to the following conditions:

(a) Retain the above copyright notice and this license.
(b) Clearly identify Motive as the source of the code used.

This permission applies only to project code. It does not grant permission
to use texture assets or model assets, which are governed by Sections 2 and 3,
respectively.

2. Texture Assets

Permission is granted to use, copy, modify, and distribute the project's
texture assets without requesting separate permission, subject to all of
the following conditions:

(a) Retain the above copyright notice and this license.
(b) Clearly identify Motive as the source of the texture assets used.
(c) Clearly and explicitly acknowledge the use of Motive texture assets in
    the recipient project's public documentation, release page, or public
    credits.

A hidden comment alone does not satisfy the public acknowledgment requirement.
Permission to use a texture asset does not grant permission to use any
associated model asset.

3. Model Assets - All Rights Reserved (ARR)

All rights in the project's model assets are reserved by their respective
rights holders. Except as permitted by applicable law, anyone other than the
relevant rights holder must request and obtain prior express permission
from that rights holder, or an author authorized to grant such permission,
before using, copying, modifying, extracting, distributing, or incorporating
model assets into another project.

Public display, availability for download, or access to source files does
not, by itself, grant permission to use model assets. No permission to use
model assets is granted under Sections 1 or 2.

Permission to use a model asset does not transfer ownership. The scope of
permitted use is limited to the express permission granted by the relevant
rights holder or authorized author.

4. Ownership and Attribution

Permission to use project code or assets does not transfer copyright or
permit false claims of original authorship. Attribution must identify the
original Motive material and must not misrepresent it as the recipient's
original work.

Model assets remain the property of their respective rights holders unless
those rights holders expressly agree otherwise. Rights not expressly granted
by this license are reserved, subject to applicable law.

5. Disclaimer

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE PROJECT CODE AND ASSETS
ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES. THE AUTHORS
AND RIGHTS HOLDERS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR LOSSES ARISING FROM THE USE OF
THE PROJECT CODE OR ASSETS.

